sentences.text:
The petitioners have challenged the findings of the award and value of the structure on various grounds:- that the LAC has miserably failed to assess the market value according to its situation and potential value of the land; that there was no place in Delhi where price of land was less than Rs.1 lac per sq. yards;
that the LAC did not consider the potential value of the land at the time of assessing its market value; that the land of the petitioners was surrounded with posh colonies such as Navin Shahdara,
Krishna Nagar, Bhola Nath Nagar, Gandhi Nagar, Mansarovar Garden, Dilshad Garden, Shyam Lal College and Vishwas Nagar Industrial Area; that cinema malls, hospitals, public schools were also there and Shahdara Railway Sttaion was also situated within the limits of land of the petitioners;
that all civic amenities such as water, sewer, electricity, telephone, markets etc. were available to the land of the petitioners; that the entire land of the petitioner was built up and there were Dharamshala, community halls etc; that the LAC should have fixed Rs.1 lac per sq. yards, as market value of the land and Rs.5 lacs should have been fixed, being value of the structure; that the LAC has wrongly relied upon the schedule of rates of land of Delhi, fixed for 1996 and he should have considered the same, which have been increased 10 times from 1996 to 1999.
